; What the DOS runtime defines (Game_dosrt.c, llasm/Game-llasm.llasm) for the
; translated code of a DOS4GW game; the game's extern.llinc includes this.

; The privileged-register and descriptor-table shadows that `mov cr0`, `lsl`,
; `smsw` and `sidt` are rewritten to load and store (instruction_replacements.sci).
; Game_DosIdtBase points at a ~2 KB buffer, a fake IDT never dispatched through.
extern Game_DosCr0
extern Game_DosDsLimit
extern Game_DosIdtBase

; The environment of the program as the C library reads it: the guest address
; of the array of the addresses of the variables ("NAME=VALUE"), a zero at its
; end.  WATCOM's start-up builds its own; a game that starts at its main skips
; that, and its instruction_replacements.sci loads this one instead.
extern Game_DosEnviron

; The drivers of the Miles AIL/32 2.x (llasm/ail2.llinc): external_procedures.sci
; routes AIL_register_driver and the dispatcher of the driver functions to them.
proc SR_AIL2_register_driver external
proc SR_AIL2_call_driver external
; DSMI's MCP on the host (Game_dosdsmi.c, GAME_DOS_DSMI): the game's
; instruction_replacements.sci calls them in place of MCP's getdelta and poll.
func Game_DsmiMcpGetDelta
func Game_DsmiMcpPoll microseconds, vars, order
